This fork is based on upstream tag v2.0.7. Modifications made by BRILIA fall into
six kinds, and are released under the same Apache License, Version 2.0:

1. Changes to BEHAVIOUR, made for Windows compatibility. How the hook command is
   written, quoted and launched changes on Windows only; the parser that
   recognises this plugin's own hook command also accepts the double-quoted form
   on every platform. These carry the prominent notice required by section 4(b)
   of the License, at the top of each file that holds them:
   runtime/hooks/install-paths.ts, runtime/commands/setup.ts, and
   tests/runtime/install-paths.test.ts, plus their compiled counterparts under
   dist/ and plugins/k3-codex/dist/.

2. Changes to IDENTITY, so that a fork can be distributed without claiming to be
   the upstream project, and can be installed beside it: the plugin and
   marketplace names, the version string, and the renaming from the upstream
   namespace to ours of commands, agents, Codex skills, environment variables,
   the marker of the hook block, the data directory and the messages. The
   renaming is mechanical and defined in one place, scripts/identity-map.mjs.
   Applied to an upstream file, the map yields ours byte for byte, except for
   the files it lists in DECLARED_DIVERGENT with the reason, all of which are
   covered by the other kinds below (`node scripts/identity-map.mjs verify
   v2.0.7` checks this). Because the renaming is applied consistently, the code
   that recognises its own install tree, data directory and hook block now
   recognises this fork's and not upstream's; in that sense it is not inert,
   and kind 6 describes what follows from it.

3. ADDITIONS that upstream does not carry: three manual test harnesses
   (tests/manual/enforcement-matrix.mjs,
   tests/manual/shell-probe-discrimination.mjs and
   tests/manual/coexistence-smoke.mjs, which installs upstream and this fork
   side by side in a temporary home), two maintainer scripts
   (scripts/promote-to-main.mjs and scripts/identity-map.mjs) with their tests
   (tests/scripts/), and this fork's documentation.

4. Changes to RELEASE AND CI plumbing. This fork is not published to npm:
   upstream's .github/workflows/publish.yml is removed, package.json is private
   and points to this repository. CI also runs on staging/** branches, because
   this repository requires a green CI run on a commit before main may point at
   it.

5. A RELIABILITY FIX on every platform, in runtime/job-store.ts,
   runtime/jobs.ts and runtime/commands/repair-sessions.ts (each with the
   prominent notice of section 4(b) at the top, plus their compiled
   counterparts): the job store sets busy_timeout before journal_mode = WAL, so
   opening it while another process holds the database waits up to 5 seconds
   instead of failing at once with SQLITE_BUSY; the background wait keeps
   polling past a busy store until its own deadline; and the read-only
   connection used by repair-sessions sets the same busy timeout. Regression
   tests: tests/runtime/job-store-busy-open.test.ts, with the helpers
   tests/helpers/hold-exclusive-lock.ts and tests/helpers/open-job-store-node.mjs.

6. A MIGRATION from this fork's own releases up to 0.5.x, which still used
   upstream's names, on every platform. runtime/plugin-data.ts recognises this
   fork's install layout; runtime/paths.ts names the data directory
   k3-plugin-cc and keeps using the old kimi-plugin-cc directory while only
   that one exists; runtime/commands/setup.ts removes this fork's own hook
   blocks under the old marker (never another plugin's), moves the data
   directory when no job is running, leaving under the old name an alias that a
   later setup removes, rewrites the paths stored for past jobs, and reports the
   old environment variables, which are not read; runtime/job-store.ts gains the
   two methods that move needs. Each carries the prominent notice of section 4(b) at the top, as do
   their compiled counterparts. Added files: runtime/hooks/legacy-brand.ts,
   runtime/legacy-names.ts, tests/runtime/legacy-brand.test.ts,
   tests/scripts/identity-map.test.js and tests/scripts/brand-residue.test.js.

